/Title (The significance of this story in Indonesian culture lies in its representation of the power of love and the consequences of breaking a curse. It also highlights the importance of trust and honesty in relationships. The story has been passed down through generations in Javanese culture, and it continues to be a beloved part of Indonesian folklore.)
